  "author": "A Robot",
  "institution": "MTSU",
  "courseName": "Introductory Molecular Biology",
  "estimatedLength": "25 minutes",
  "objectives": [
    "Identify the major structural components of DNA, including sugar-phosphate backbones, nitrogenous bases, and hydrogen bonds, and relate these parts to the double helix.",
    "Apply complementary base-pairing rules to infer a DNA strand sequence from its template and explain the bonding differences between A-T and G-C pairs.",
    "Explain how 5' to 3' backbone directionality produces antiparallel DNA strands.",
    "Trace the roles of helicase, single-strand binding proteins, DNA polymerase, and DNA ligase during DNA replication.",
    "Distinguish leading-strand and lagging-strand synthesis and connect their differences to the 5' to 3' constraint on DNA polymerase.",
    "Explain why DNA replication is semiconservative and predict the strand composition of daughter DNA molecules after replication."
  ],
